quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  43,11,"and Who sent down water from the sky in perfect measure, and We revived with it a dead land. Thus shall you be brought forth (from the dead)."
  43,12,"And Who created all the pairs, and made for you ships and animals that you ride,"
  43,13,"so that you may mount their backs and remember the blessing of your Lord, when you are settled on them, and say: ‘Glory be to Him, Who has subjected this for us, and we (on our own) were no match for it."
  43,14,And indeed we shall return to our Lord.’
  43,15,"Yet they (the polytheists) assign a portion from among His servants (as His offspring) to Him. Verily, humankind is manifestly ungrateful."
  43,16,Did He adopt (for Himself) daughters from what He created while He preferred you with sons?
  43,17,"Whenever one of them is given the news of what he attributes to the Most-Compassionate (i.e. the birth of a daughter), his face blackens as he suppresses his anger."
  43,18,What! (Do they attribute to Him that) which is reared amid ornaments and cannot articulate a clear argument.*
  43,19,"Still, they have classed the angels, who are the servants of the Most-Compassionate (Lord), as females. Did they witness their creation? Their testimony shall be written down, and they shall be interrogated (on the Last Day)."
  43,20,"They (further) say: ‘Had the Most-Compassionate (Lord) wished, we would not have worshipped these (idols).’ They have no knowledge (in support) of this (claim). And they only tell lies out of fancy."
  43,21,"Did We give them a Book before this, so they are holding fast to it?"
  43,22,"Rather, they say: ‘We found our fathers following a creed, and we are following in their footsteps.’"
